frosted separable Gaussian: no encoders in steady frames (the title bar's backdrop key is constant, so the cached blur is bound).

RISK (Oracle, on merge 39cdb5c): the backdrop key is a Debug hash of the prior Paint ops (+ time when one is
time-driven). Anything that reaches the backdrop WITHOUT changing a prior op is invisible to it: a texture
sampled by an earlier op whose contents change (a live pane cell texture, an image), or pixels drawn outside
encode_ops (a host draw hook) before the frosted op. Then a frosted surface would show a stale blur. Today the
only frosted surface, the title bar, paints first over the static background, so nothing like that precedes it.
Mitigation when it can happen (modals or the launcher over live panes, Aster's retained cell textures): the
host folds a content generation for every external texture or hook into the key, or passes no key for
frosted ops that follow them.
